E='gortereghy-elder-households-1911'
finding('irish-gortereghy-james-elder-family-age-conflict-1901','The original 1901 return names James Elder 80, wife Mary 73, daughter Lizzie 25 and son William 23. William and Elizabeth are a proved sibling pair in 1911, aged 40 and 50. These are substantial original-record age conflicts, not index errors. Elder-3951 and Elder-3950 remain compatible together, while identifying the 1901 children with the 1911 pair and attaching the latter to Elder-3946 remains uncertain.',['nai000298444','nai001390136'],[(E,'william-elder'),(E,'elizabeth-elder')])
for ch in ['Lizzie Elder, 25, 1901','William Elder, 23, 1901']:R(ch,'James Elder / Mary, Gortereghy 1901','documented father and mother in original return',['nai000298444'],ids='James Elder-3946 / Mary Jane McAughin compatible; 1901-to-1911 child continuity uncertain')
M='gortereghy-mccaughern-household-1911'
finding('irish-gortereghy-sarah-mccaughern-continuity-1901','The original 1901 and 1911 returns establish continuity of Sarah McCaughern’s Gortereghy family. Sarah was a Derry-born widow aged 72/82; Caroline, Sarah J/Sara Jane, James A/Jas Alex, Matilda and grandson George occur in both returns. Elizabeth, 32, is also a daughter in 1901. Sarah Dysart-1893, married in 1851 to Gortereghy farmer John McCaughern, remains the strongest mother identity, but neither census names her deceased husband or maiden surname.',['nai000298441','nai001390134','dysart-1851'],[(M,p) for p in ['sarah-mccaughern','matilda-mulholland','caroline-mccaughern','sara-jane-mccaughern','jas-alex-mccaughern','geo-mulholland']])
finding('irish-matilda-adir-mulholland-separate-1901','Original returns place Matilda Adair, 32, with four Adair sons and grandmother Ester Mulhollond in Monkstown Village, while Matilda M’Choland, 45, is a married daughter in Sarah McCaughern’s Gortereghy household on the same 1901 census night. Their different simultaneous family groups and ages distinguish Mulholland-1040 from the Gortereghy daughter.',['nai000358901','nai000298441'],[(M,'matilda-mulholland')])
for p,text,key in [('thomas-ross','The original 1901 Gortereghy return describes Thomas Ross, 34, as farmer and flax miller, with Scotland-born wife Mary Jane and six children. This supplies an occupation bridge to the 1912 mill-owner directory entry; the 1911 return records 24 years of marriage and seven surviving children. Ross-13124 remains compatible; the reported census ages differ.', 'nai000298459'),('peter-mccaughern','The original 1911 Dreen return names Peter McCaughern, 48, single Roman Catholic farmer, with his sister Agnes, 55. He is a concrete candidate for the 1912 Rasharkin grocer/farmer and later Dreen probate man, but the directory-to-household identification remains probable and no father is named.','nai001389792'),('robert-mccaughern','The original 1911 Lisnagaver return identifies Robert McCaughern, 54, farmer, with wife Mary Anne, 58; married 28 years, both Antrim-born Church of Ireland. The occupation and exact locality strongly identify the 1912 directory farmer. His parents are not stated.','nai001389352'),('john-wallace','The original 1911 Lisnagaver return identifies John Wallace, 55, National School Teacher born County Derry, with Antrim-born wife Mary Anne, 52; married 26 years, seven children born and six living. Their six resident children are Mary H, William G, James G, Samuel G, Sarah G and Letitia C. This strongly identifies the 1912 directory teacher.','nai001389399')]:
 finding('irish-'+p+'-census-family',text,[key]+(['nai001390150'] if p=='thomas-ross' else []),[('rasharkin-directory-1912',p)])
finding('irish-macaw-hugh-transcription-date-correction','Rereading Rasharkin baptism transcription entry 125 gives Hugh Macaw’s birth as 3 February 1839, replacing the maintained 5 February wording. His baptism remains 3 March 1839; original manuscript inspection is required before treating the corrected transcription as a final date.',['macaw-register'],[('lisnagaver-macaw-kilpatrick-1839',p) for p in ['hugh-macaw','william-macaw','mary-kilpatrick']],qualification='Named transcription reread; original manuscript uninspected.')
# Specific row arguments, questions and source amendments.
custom={
(G,'robert-elder-father'):('Elder-7144 remains compatible for the living 1901 father of Alex/Robert/Eliza/Margaretta; its 1827 birth is tree-derived and differs from reported age 65, so retain uncertainty. Elder-7251 represents Mary Glasgow’s separate Gortahar family: she is a widow there in 1901 while the Gortereghy Robert is alive. Do not exclude Elder-7251 globally from Sarah’s 1893 father clause merely because a father can be deceased at marriage. Sarah and Isaac’s father occurrences remain unproved bridges to the 1901 family. The original 1881 Jane birth proves Robert/Jane Calderwood as a parental couple, not the mother identity of all later siblings.','Find original births/marriages identifying the 1901 siblings and the 1901 father’s death; compare the Jane Calderwood family before making any certain profile attachment.'),
(G,'alexander-elder'):('The original 1901 Alex is explicitly Robert’s son; the 1911 return names brother Robert and sister Margaret. Together with the 1908 Alexander/Mary Anderson marriage extract, these support one sibling family. Retain the actual age differences. Use the same qualified Elder-7144 father hypothesis for Alexander and proved siblings; mother Jane on the memorial is separately evidenced, while Jane Calderwood remains a comparison. No matching Alexander profile was established in full same-name and father-filtered searches.','Inspect original 1908 marriage and a matching birth/death to secure Elder-7144 identity and mother’s maiden surname.'),
(G,'robert-elder-brother'):('The 1901 return proves younger Robert a son of Robert Elder; the 1911 return proves him Alexander’s brother. Elder-1585 (c1869, unsourced father Robert/Christina) and Elder-4828 (1871 Inch/Canada, unsourced tree family) remain weak unplaced candidates: unsupported birth and parents alone cannot exclude them. Elder-7303 is concretely a separate simultaneous Gortahar household son of Mary in 1901 and head with mother Mary in 1911. Extend Alexander’s qualified Elder-7144 father hypothesis across the documentary siblings; do not assert certain profile identity.','Check the weak candidates’ dated life records and original birth/marriage of the Gortereghy Robert; preserve 1901 age20 versus 1911 age34.'),
(M,'sarah-mccaughern'):('Original 1901/1911 returns prove household continuity, widowhood and Derry birth. The original 1851 Sarah Dysart/John McCaughern marriage supplies locality and generation compatibility; Sarah’s minor status conflicts slightly with an 1829 birth inferred from census age82, so treat ages as reported and retain Dysart-1893 as probable-compatible rather than matched. No census names husband or maiden surname. If the identity is retained, carry John McCaughern-23 as the same uncertain father hypothesis across the proved siblings; their mother relationship to documentary Sarah is certain.','Seek at least one original birth of Caroline/Sara Jane/James Alexander/Elizabeth naming Sarah Dysart and John; civil collection form blocked at Section61, so no completed civil search is claimed.'),
(M,'matilda-mulholland'):('Mulholland-1040 is excluded from this Gortereghy daughter by two inspected simultaneous 1901 family returns, not by absent parents. The Gortereghy Matilda is age45 married in 1901 and52 widow in1911; the Monkstown Matilda is32, married Adair, with sons9/8/3/1. Preserve the reported age disagreement45→52. Documentary Sarah is her proved mother; Dysart-1893 and John McCaughern-23 may be carried together as an explicitly uncertain family identity. George is Sarah’s grandson, not explicitly Matilda’s son.','Find Matilda’s original marriage and George’s original birth before assigning her husband or making the inferred Matilda/George parent-child link certain.'),
('rasharkin-john-elder-marriages','annie-patterson'):('The inspected 1886 register proves Annie Patterson age20, daughter of David Patterson farmer, marrying grocer John Elder (Elder-5907 exact event match). Family-filtered search recovers Patterson-32389 Anne Jane (baptism-derived1860, Ballyculter, fatherDavid miner) and Patterson-14390 Annie1858 (unsourced Ontario tree, fatherDavid): retain both as weak candidates, with reported ages, father occupations and locality differences explicit. Those differences alone do not prove incompatible life courses.','Inspect candidate life records and Annie’s original birth/1911 household; do not create an orphan bride while these candidates remain plausible.'),
('rasharkin-john-elder-marriages','peggy-stuart'):('Stuart-11578 remains an undated Antrim candidate; fatherJames in that profile is a lead, not proved by the witness James Stuart in1842. Stewart-53456 is now concretely excluded: her original1848 marriage calls her SPINSTER, inconsistent with being John Elder’s1842 wife. Preserve the separate1842 subject.','Inspect the original1842 church register and original life records for Stuart-11578.'),
('rasharkin-john-elder-marriages','john-elder'):('Split the queue into1842John/Peggy,1886John/Annie,1912grocer-postmaster. Elder-5907 matches the inspected1886grocer marriage and remains strongly compatible for1912. Elder-7230 and Elder-4387 remain weak older candidates for1842; no evidence identifies1842John as5907’s father. The original1886fatherJohn is certain within that record, while his profile identity remains unknown.','Inspect original1842marriage and a source linking the1886fatherJohn to an older candidate. Do not retire the entire queue because1886is matched.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','thomas-ross'):('1901original farmer/flax-miller ThomasRoss with MaryJane provides a strong bridge to1912Gortreighymillowner;1911samefamily married24years. Ross-13124(1867Whitehouse) remains compatible but notproved. Ross-29596(1874civil-birthcitation) has severe chronology tension: would be12–13at1886/7marriage and about11when1901Jeannie15wasborn; directbirthPDFHTTP403prevented freshverification, so retain as weak conditionalcandidate ratherthanclaimoriginal-based exclusion. Ross-25888has a separate Gransha/AnnJane family; Ross-29600is RobertT.Ross,died1909.','Inspect Ross-29596birthimage and originalThomas/MaryJanemarriage toresolve fatherandcandidateidentity.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','peter-mccaughern'):('Original1911DreenPeter48and sisterAgnes55supply a concrete family/context for the1912farmer/grocer. Probablecontinuitywith1916Dreenprobatesremainsqualified; originalprobatePDFnotinspected inthislane. SearchesMcCaughern/McCaughan/McCarnagh plusMcCahernvariant identifiednoprofile. Noactualfathernameis evidenced.','Compareoriginal1916probateandPeterdeathwiththe1911household; do notinventaparentfromWilliamadministrator.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','robert-mccaughern'):('The inspected1911Lisnagaverfarmer54wifeMaryAnne58married28yearsstronglyidentifies1912directoryRobert. McCaughan-13remainsunplacedname-onlylead withundated/unsourcedparents ratherthananexcludedidentity. ExactMcCaughern/McCarnagh/McCahern searchesreturnedzero; noexistingcompatibleidentityestablished. MaryAnnepossiblyMcCaughern-24cannotbeexcludedoridentifiedsolelybysameageandname.','Seekoriginalcirca1883marriageforRobert/MaryAnneusingbothsurnames andvariants; inspecttheirparentclausesbeforeextendingSarahDysartfamily.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','john-wallace'):('Original1911teacherhouseholdstronglyidentifiesdirectoryJohn, bornDerryabout1856,wifeMaryAnne,marriedabout1884–85. Wallace-17947andWallace-3457retainweakcandidatequalification; sourcelevelofclaimedKilwaughter/Ballynurebirthsdoesnotjustifyexcludingbyplacealone. RefinedWallace-26687dies1880asasinglestudent, aconcreteconflictwithliving1911teacher.','Inspectteacher’soriginalmarriage and candidatebirth/deathrecords; usewifeMaryAnneandchildrenMaryH/WilliamG/JamesG/SamuelG/SarahG/LetitiaC.'),
('prescott-rochester-james-family','alexander-glasco'):('ReviewedoriginalC114provesAlexanderGlascoexpressagent sonJamesformerlyPrescottcarpenter. Glasgow-951iscompatibleonlywithsubstantialIrish/Canadianidentityuncertainty; propertyoccupancydoesnotprovephysicalresidencein1868. NewRochesternewspaperindexAlexanderdeathlead29August1892needsactualarticleandoccupation/familybeforeitcanconflictwith951’s1888death. Nooriginalnewspaperarticlewasfound.','ReadUnionandAdvertiser29August1892p5col6andUS/Canadacensus; compare expressagent fatherJames before any951 identification.'),
('prescott-rochester-james-family','james-glasgow'):('B395/B601/C114consolidatethree explicitlynamedchildrenofJamescarpenter:ElizaJane,MaryandAlexanderexpressagent. RobertGlasgow-4150’sbrotherJamesisapropertyhypothesis, notprovedprofileidentity. Keeponefamilydraftwithdirectfatherties; fractionscannotestablishcompletechildcount. FullGlasgow/Glascoandvariantsearchesfoundnosupportedexistingcarpenterprofile; unplacedGlasgow-3743leadisnotexcludedonlybydifferentgeography.','InspectRochester1893Jamesdeatharticles and Prescott/Rochestercensus toidentifyparentsandconnecttheknown siblings withoutcreatingonepersonperdeed.')}
# Replace condensed phrases with readable prose in durable output.
def readable(s):
 import re
 return re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z])(?=[A-Z])',' ',s)
entries=[];patches=[]
for old in a['entries']:
 e=copy.deepcopy(old);g=e['group_slug'];p=e['subject_anchor'];key=(g,p);baseline=people[key];si=config[g][1][:]
 if key in custom:e['argument'],nextq=custom[key];e['argument']=readable(e['argument']);nextq=readable(nextq)
